Find the smallest positive value of \(a\) such that the equation \[
\sqrt{x^2 + (y - a)^2} = \sqrt{2} \cdot \sqrt{x^2 + (y + a)^2}
\] has exactly one real and nonnegative solution for \(y\) when \(x = 0\). Express your answer as a common fraction.

Find the number of solutions to the equation \( k^2 - 3k + 2 = 0 \) and identify which values of \( k \) ensure the columns of the matrix \[
\begin{bmatrix}
1 & k \\
2 & 4 \\
\end{bmatrix}
\] are linearly independent.

Find all positive integers \(x\) that satisfy the following system of congruences:
\[
\begin{cases}
x \equiv 3 \pmod{5} \\
x \equiv 4 \pmod{7} \\
x \equiv 11 \cdot n - 1 \pmod{11}
\end{cases}
\]
where \(n\) is a non-negative integer.
